WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.650
Imagine you are waiting for a bus.

2
00:00:02.660 --> 00:00:07.410
It leaves at nine fifteen and reaches your
destination at ten oh five.

3
00:00:07.450 --> 00:00:11.720
You glance at the clock and wonder, how
long did the journey really take?

4
00:00:11.730 --> 00:00:13.410
Could it be ten minutes?

5
00:00:13.470 --> 00:00:15.980
Or is there something we are missing?

6
00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:17.870
Let us find out together.

7
00:00:18.935 --> 00:00:23.195
Today we are learning how to read time and
calculate duration.

8
00:00:23.235 --> 00:00:27.845
Welcome to MathMagic, where we explore
mathematics using everyday puzzles,

9
00:00:27.845 --> 00:00:29.995
clear pictures, and smart thinking.

10
00:00:30.035 --> 00:00:34.045
By the end, you will be able to solve our
bus mystery yourself.

11
00:00:35.053 --> 00:00:39.343
Our learning goal is to read time
accurately, calculate elapsed time, and

12
00:00:39.343 --> 00:00:42.313
explain our thinking using clocks and
timelines.

13
00:00:43.315 --> 00:00:48.025
By the end, you can read the hour and
minute hands, calculate a duration

14
00:00:48.025 --> 00:00:51.375
that crosses the hour, and check your
answer with a timeline.

15
00:00:52.388 --> 00:00:54.258
Start with the minute hand.

16
00:00:54.268 --> 00:00:57.598
Each large step around the clock is five
minutes.

17
00:00:57.618 --> 00:01:01.388
The minute hand at three means fifteen
minutes past the hour.

18
00:01:02.417 --> 00:01:04.697
Now find the short hour hand.

19
00:01:04.737 --> 00:01:08.957
It sits a little after nine, because
fifteen minutes of the ninth hour have

20
00:01:08.957 --> 00:01:11.987
passed. This clock shows nine fifteen.

21
00:01:13.002 --> 00:01:14.432
Look at this clock.

22
00:01:14.472 --> 00:01:16.222
What time does it show?

23
00:01:16.252 --> 00:01:19.362
Read the minute hand first, then the hour
hand.

24
00:01:19.392 --> 00:01:22.192
Give yourself five seconds to decide.

25
00:01:27.195 --> 00:01:30.605
The minute hand points to eight, or forty
minutes.

26
00:01:30.645 --> 00:01:33.545
The hour hand is between three and four.

27
00:01:33.596 --> 00:01:36.446
It is three forty, not eight fifteen.

28
00:01:37.469 --> 00:01:39.679
Let's return to our bus journey.

29
00:01:39.679 --> 00:01:43.519
It begins at nine fifteen and finishes at
ten oh five.

30
00:01:43.559 --> 00:01:47.569
We can make the calculation easier by
jumping to the next hour.

31
00:01:48.616 --> 00:01:52.346
From nine fifteen to ten o'clock, how many
minutes pass?

32
00:01:52.356 --> 00:01:56.286
You could count in fives, or subtract
fifteen from sixty.

33
00:02:01.306 --> 00:02:05.386
Forty-five minutes pass between nine
fifteen and ten o'clock.

34
00:02:05.396 --> 00:02:07.846
That is our first part of the journey.

35
00:02:08.846 --> 00:02:13.776
Then the bus travels another five minutes,
from ten o'clock to ten oh five.

36
00:02:13.796 --> 00:02:15.226
We add the two parts:

37
00:02:15.226 --> 00:02:18.096
forty-five plus five equals fifty minutes.

38
00:02:19.112 --> 00:02:23.742
A common mistake is to subtract fifteen
from five and say the journey took

39
00:02:23.742 --> 00:02:27.122
ten minutes. That ignores the change of
hour.

40
00:02:27.142 --> 00:02:29.972
A timeline makes the missing minutes
visible.

41
00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:33.830
Now let's read twenty-four-hour time.

42
00:02:33.890 --> 00:02:37.940
Nine fifteen in the morning is written
zero nine fifteen.

43
00:02:37.980 --> 00:02:41.660
Three forty in the afternoon is written
fifteen forty.

44
00:02:42.649 --> 00:02:46.359
For afternoon times after twelve, add
twelve to the hour.

45
00:02:46.389 --> 00:02:48.829
Three plus twelve equals fifteen.

46
00:02:48.859 --> 00:02:50.809
The minutes do not change.

47
00:02:51.835 --> 00:02:55.985
A movie begins at thirteen twenty and ends
at fourteen ten.

48
00:02:56.015 --> 00:02:58.395
Before I reveal the answer, estimate:

49
00:02:58.395 --> 00:03:01.995
is the duration closer to thirty minutes
or one hour?

50
00:03:07.061 --> 00:03:10.991
From thirteen twenty to fourteen hundred
is forty minutes.

51
00:03:11.011 --> 00:03:14.131
Another ten minutes takes us to fourteen
ten.

52
00:03:14.181 --> 00:03:16.301
The total is fifty minutes.

53
00:03:17.320 --> 00:03:19.250
Here is a useful trick.

54
00:03:19.290 --> 00:03:23.150
A clock has sixty minutes, but only twelve
large numbers.

55
00:03:23.150 --> 00:03:27.430
Each jump between two neighbouring numbers
represents five minutes.

56
00:03:27.430 --> 00:03:31.950
Start at twelve and count five, ten,
fifteen, twenty, twenty-five, and

57
00:03:31.950 --> 00:03:32.510
thirty.

58
00:03:33.507 --> 00:03:36.207
Take a look at this clock showing six
thirty.

59
00:03:36.207 --> 00:03:39.347
Before you hear my answer, point to the
minute hand.

60
00:03:39.367 --> 00:03:42.287
Why does it point to six instead of
thirty?

61
00:03:42.287 --> 00:03:46.157
Pause and think about what each large
number represents.

62
00:03:51.157 --> 00:03:55.607
The long minute hand points to six, which
represents thirty minutes.

63
00:03:55.637 --> 00:03:59.307
The shorter hour hand is halfway between
six and seven.

64
00:03:59.337 --> 00:04:02.017
Half past six is written six thirty.

65
00:04:02.017 --> 00:04:06.207
We never read the number under the minute
hand as the minutes directly.

66
00:04:07.209 --> 00:04:09.499
We can also use the word quarter.

67
00:04:09.539 --> 00:04:12.599
A quarter of sixty minutes is fifteen
minutes.

68
00:04:12.639 --> 00:04:16.379
When the minute hand points to three, it
is quarter past the hour.

69
00:04:16.389 --> 00:04:19.529
When it points to nine, it is quarter to
the next hour.

70
00:04:20.534 --> 00:04:23.124
This clock shows nine forty-five.

71
00:04:23.164 --> 00:04:26.264
Is that quarter past nine, or quarter to
ten?

72
00:04:26.304 --> 00:04:29.874
Look closely at where the shorter hour
hand is moving.

73
00:04:29.904 --> 00:04:32.694
Give yourself five seconds to decide.

74
00:04:37.720 --> 00:04:39.430
It is quarter to ten.

75
00:04:39.470 --> 00:04:43.480
Forty-five minutes have already passed
since nine o'clock, and fifteen

76
00:04:43.480 --> 00:04:45.240
minutes remain until ten.

77
00:04:45.270 --> 00:04:47.820
The hour hand is nearly at ten.

78
00:04:47.850 --> 00:04:50.380
That is why we say quarter to ten.

79
00:04:51.402 --> 00:04:55.672
To calculate a duration, we are not
looking for the difference between two

80
00:04:55.672 --> 00:05:00.232
clock numbers. We want the amount of time
that actually passes.

81
00:05:00.262 --> 00:05:04.332
A number line or timeline shows each part
of the journey clearly.

82
00:05:05.318 --> 00:05:08.738
Think of ten o'clock as a friendly
stopping point.

83
00:05:08.748 --> 00:05:12.028
First travel from nine fifteen to ten
o'clock.

84
00:05:12.028 --> 00:05:15.278
Then travel from ten o'clock to ten oh
five.

85
00:05:15.298 --> 00:05:19.528
We can add the two durations because the
parts do not overlap.

86
00:05:20.565 --> 00:05:25.265
Try another example. A swimming lesson
begins at two twenty-five

87
00:05:25.265 --> 00:05:26.965
and finishes at three ten.

88
00:05:26.985 --> 00:05:29.675
How many minutes until three o'clock?

89
00:05:29.735 --> 00:05:32.635
Then how many more minutes until three
ten?

90
00:05:32.665 --> 00:05:35.125
Work it out before the explanation.

91
00:05:40.133 --> 00:05:44.313
From two twenty-five to three o'clock is
thirty-five minutes.

92
00:05:44.333 --> 00:05:48.063
From three o'clock to three ten is another
ten minutes.

93
00:05:48.073 --> 00:05:51.733
Thirty-five plus ten equals forty-five
minutes.

94
00:05:51.763 --> 00:05:54.913
The swimming lesson lasts forty-five
minutes.

95
00:05:55.935 --> 00:05:58.585
Check the reasonableness of your answer.

96
00:05:58.645 --> 00:06:03.095
If an activity begins before three o'clock
and finishes just after three

97
00:06:03.095 --> 00:06:06.465
o'clock, a duration of five minutes is too
short.

98
00:06:06.475 --> 00:06:09.995
Estimate first, then calculate to catch
mistakes.

99
00:06:11.010 --> 00:06:14.360
Now let us compare morning and afternoon
times.

100
00:06:14.380 --> 00:06:18.850
A digital clock may show three forty in
the afternoon, while a twenty-four-

101
00:06:18.850 --> 00:06:20.860
hour clock shows fifteen forty.

102
00:06:20.900 --> 00:06:24.150
Both represent exactly the same moment.

103
00:06:25.141 --> 00:06:26.811
Here is a quick check.

104
00:06:26.831 --> 00:06:31.051
If a sports match starts at fourteen
twenty, what time is that on a twelve-

105
00:06:31.051 --> 00:06:34.921
hour clock? Think about subtracting twelve
from the hour.

106
00:06:34.921 --> 00:06:37.601
The minutes should stay exactly the same.

107
00:06:42.636 --> 00:06:47.296
Fourteen minus twelve equals two, so
fourteen twenty is two twenty

108
00:06:47.296 --> 00:06:52.006
in the afternoon. Notice that we did not
subtract twelve from the minutes.

109
00:06:52.006 --> 00:06:54.666
The twenty minutes remain twenty minutes.

110
00:06:55.654 --> 00:06:57.674
Be careful around midday.

111
00:06:57.695 --> 00:07:01.464
Twelve noon is twelve hundred in
twenty-four-hour time.

112
00:07:01.505 --> 00:07:03.685
Midnight is zero hundred.

113
00:07:03.744 --> 00:07:08.044
These two moments are twelve hours apart,
even though both may be written as

114
00:07:08.044 --> 00:07:10.164
twelve on a twelve-hour clock.

115
00:07:11.160 --> 00:07:14.070
Here is our final independent challenge.

116
00:07:14.080 --> 00:07:18.790
A train leaves at eleven thirty-five and
reaches its destination at twelve

117
00:07:18.790 --> 00:07:21.100
twenty. How long does it travel?

118
00:07:21.260 --> 00:07:25.590
Draw a timeline with noon as the middle
stop and solve each part.

119
00:07:30.600 --> 00:07:34.440
From eleven thirty-five to noon is
twenty-five minutes.

120
00:07:34.460 --> 00:07:37.910
From noon to twelve twenty is another
twenty minutes.

121
00:07:37.910 --> 00:07:41.610
Twenty-five plus twenty equals forty-five
minutes.

122
00:07:41.640 --> 00:07:44.450
The train journey takes forty-five
minutes.

123
00:07:45.464 --> 00:07:49.254
To check your understanding, explain the
method to someone else.

124
00:07:49.274 --> 00:07:53.684
Read the clock hands, choose a helpful
hour boundary, count each jump, and

125
00:07:53.684 --> 00:07:58.444
add the minutes. If your answer seems
surprising, draw the timeline again.

126
00:07:59.481 --> 00:08:03.921
Today you read clock hands, crossed an
hour boundary, and converted between

127
00:08:03.921 --> 00:08:06.381
twelve-hour and twenty-four-hour time.

128
00:08:06.401 --> 00:08:10.491
Remember: count the time between the two
moments, not just the numbers on

129
00:08:10.491 --> 00:08:11.291
the clock.

130
00:08:12.290 --> 00:08:16.820
Your challenge: a train departs at eleven
thirty-five and arrives at twelve

131
00:08:16.820 --> 00:08:21.490
twenty. Draw a timeline, find the
duration, and explain each jump.

132
00:08:21.560 --> 00:08:24.230
Then try the MathMagic practice.
